[U]/D[U]}`","source_id":"loongarch-vol1","text":"```\n    GR[rd] = unsigned(GR[rj][63:0]) % unsigned(GR[rk][63:0])\n```\n\nWhen `DIV.W` , `MOD.W` , `DIV.D` and `MOD.D` perform division operations, the operands are all regarded as signed numbers. When `DIV.WU` , `M0D.WU` , `DIV.DU` and `MOD.DU` perform division operations, the source operands are all regarded as unsigned numbers.\n\nEach pair of instructions for finding the quotient/remainder satisfies the result of `DIV.W` / `MOD.W` , `DIV.WU` / `MOD.WU` , `DIV.D` / `MOD.D` , `DIV.DU` / `MOD.DU` , the remainder and the dividend The sign is consistent and the absolute value of the remainder is less than the absolute value of the divisor.\n\nWhen the divisor is `0` , the result can be any value, but no exception will be triggered."}],"query":{"id":"q015","intent":"Determine the operand interpretation and result of high-half integer multiplication.","text":"How do LoongArch MULH.D and MULH.DU interpret their operands?"}},"pilot":false,"schema":{"$defs":{"Grade":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"architecture_tags":{"items":{"enum":["riscv","loongarch","x86","other"],"type":"string"},"title":"Architecture Tags","type":"array"},"grade":{"maximum":3,"minimum":0,"title":"Grade","type":"integer"},"passage_id":{"minLength":1,"title":"Passage Id","type":"string"},"quote":{"title":"Quote","type":"string"},"reason":{"minLength":1,"title":"Reason","type":"string"}},"required":["passage_id","grade","reason","quote","architecture_tags"],"title":"Grade","type":"object"}},"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"grades":{"items":{"$ref":"#/$defs/Grade"},"title":"Grades","type":"array"}},"required":["grades"],"title":"GradeAnswer","type":"object"},"schema_version":3,"sha256":"5fb5b3e04293cc49a1206ce9ef32cccee1da111d1d6af32a347d46cebe9eb401","system_sha256":"0731bfffd8dfd9b1a7f3394b7f28e0c875dbee813b796de4afe0936d756fea63"}
